00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.910
Yeah, that looks nice.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.440
So one of the things that
makes these different

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.600
than other tile trackers
is this has access

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.690
to the entire Find My network.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.790
And what that means is anybody who has

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.430
Find My on their phone,

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.330
you're going to be basically piggy-backing

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.870
off of other people's phones and Bluetooth

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.690
to be able to find your lost items.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.840
Now, something that's kind of cool is

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:01.120
if I lose I don't know, like my jacket

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.100
or my purse or whatever and
I mark that item as lost.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.720
And then Tyler is, you
know, wherever I left it

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.190
he ends up seeing, oh my
goodness there's a purse

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.420
and he's rummaging around

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.340
or there's one of these tags on there.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.910
It would send him a
notification that would say,

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.160
hey Justine lost this.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.990
It would take you to a webpage with

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.520
either a phone number or a message

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.570
to anybody that finds it
on a way to contact me,

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.850
to get me my last item back.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.150
That's cool.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.670
Another thing that a lot of
people were saying on Twitter

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.630
is they had a really big
concern about privacy.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.750
This is not going to be
giving away your location

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.210
or the location of anybody's phone

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.240
who actually was able to
help you find your lost item.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.870
All of that is encrypted and
completely stays private.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.810
There were also concerns
about slipping one of these

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.670
into somebody's bag or
attaching it to something

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.950
and being able to track their whereabouts.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.740
A few things to kind of
keep your mind at ease.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.730
The first thing is if Tyler

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.210
was to slip this into my backpack, Tyler.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.250
Anytime this sensed some sort of motion,

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.010
it would make a sound.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.810
It would also send a
notification to my phone

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.080
saying that there was a tag nearby

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.350
that did not belong to me.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.000
Which is kind of cool
because you can just picture

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.730
that sort of pop up that would come up

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.800
whenever you open up
somebody else's Air Pods

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.633
next to your phone.

00:06:13.633 --> 00:06:14.920
They're like, these are not your Air Pods.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.980
I imagine it's very similar to that.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.020
It's like, yo, there's a
tag nearby, it's not yours.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.010
So they definitely are
keeping that in mind

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.370
because I feel like that
is a number one concern

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.780
on anything that has
tracking capabilities.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.740
It's a combination of the Find My network

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.030
and Bluetooth that will
help you find your items.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.330
And also if you have
one of the newer iPhones

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.210
with the U1 chip enabled you'll be able

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.920
to use precision tracking.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.920
This is pretty cool because
you could take your phone

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.000
and kind of walk around

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.530
and it will direct you
right to your device.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.020
Now, something else that
kind of crossed my mind

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.720
is how incredible this is going to be

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.150
for the accessibility community.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.690
And one of my friends, James Rath

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.330
is making a video talking about

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.290
how he's going to be able to use these

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.610
as a legally blind person.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.750
So I'm so excited to see his video.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:02.070
He actually sent this little
message for us right here.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.360
- Hi, my name is James Rath.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.640
I'm a documentary
filmmaker, YouTube creator

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:07.540
and I was born legally blind.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.740
I like to share the perspective
of being visually impaired

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.170
while interacting with technology

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.460
or accessible experiences like traveling.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:14.940
One of my favorite
things about the Air Tags

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.060
like most Apple products
it's actually designed

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.310
with accessibility in mind.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.810
That means that as a blind user,

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.060
I can use the Find My app

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.170
and have everything narrated to me.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.750
Including the precision tracking.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.700
So it can give me sort of this scheme

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.580
of hot or cold or Marco
Polo to find my items.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:32.100
Which, as a blind person happens a lot.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.800
I never thought I'd say this,
but thanks to the Air Tags.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.760
I'm actually looking
forward to losing things.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.080
- Thank you for the video,
James, you're the best.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.410
Make sure you guys go
check out his channel

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.450
and subscribe and also check out his video

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.560
and say that IJ Army has sent you.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.300
So now I think it's
officially time to set these

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.673
